        "Booking always happens against Cairo's own clock. The two-and-a-half to three-and-a-half hour gap to our India-based tutors — it narrows a little once Egypt's own daylight saving kicks in for the summer — leaves a comfortable window either side, so a late-afternoon or evening lesson after school, or a weekend-morning one, suits both sides without anyone staying up unreasonably late or starting unreasonably early. Confirmations spell out the exact date and time so there's no mental arithmetic involved on your end.",
